      "hash": "29f217d5d86062d687fceaed0f8ff7da2900d2b2b33d409e4abfd6ebe310c1b4"
    },
    {
      "id": "65b8ed710617de6d300bbdeacee49a5c29e9b6fcd28bf75f77c1974ed5cd9350",
      "text": "Secondary source",
      "hash": "bfb4e03af539fffd1e5f2d37e16646bad9d6d8ed76c5e690a4111372b24e93df"
    },
    {
      "id": "c97e99ea2f55d6004511dd7a04c246b0bc66e06165e6b79b74880c4bada251c2",
      "text": "An account of a primary source, one step removed — summaries, docs, compaction summaries. Cheap to load, lossy by construction.",
      "hash": "b9bc0dd26ca1cd1e08a800a6a473e4f02e7a6e551c0ce8d3bcdb75b180fed736"
    },
    {
      "id": "44fd0b8280a82133255667161c9b32c7b7f39fefc5a95dbc26ea10acad6ca8fc",
      "text": "Matt Pocock",
      "hash": "2fe2c13509fbd45ec2578a74ef8efda313caad4f19533a102ca7d666ed60881d"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c7d1c3c7eca449951230fa8f60734828391d553411b18e79092e14368475f0d",
      "text": "Copy page",
      "hash": "4104018941ae3ab016c117887a91b4f933f28e36c587b8983373fe9377ce34d7"
    },
    {
      "id": "e1cae1b7502298f262b169c5a8d2f778edc8dbf9c9ae0ba011be1b9984e8fc00",
      "text": "An account of a",
      "hash": "0c44a351d3345bde99352f79e346f49a127891f1ac7aad71efeec3d520e69a28"
    },
    {
      "id": "455d29e8acfb594d19586ba560437d5bc1db18ed7af27b644e4571b7feee61fe",
      "text": "primary source",
      "hash": "4c3f03bb625194b79deeff56ee12d13258ff531de6eef1fff5529d0fe89a1404"
    },
    {
      "id": "29f7c0639f650c32ecc68b0e64182a71414da4b3b3a0a55fce8ca053ae5465d5",
      "text": ", one step removed — documentation describing code, a summary describing a transcript, a report describing search results. Cheaper to load into the",
      "hash": "213285a58a59b2eabfd4543dcb7da7e809f2cbcfb88ccfeac7cb946d04e76130"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae706dce481e48a21257dc4d6ed5ceca98eaa4d495f906a24169f0379613f79e",
      "text": "context window",
      "hash": "6764434518d37f01df452fe2af0af3f314f8c27a72519001ea14189c5ee42476"
    },
    {
      "id": "cfeabda3820df295b033dcc8f554efb66ec61e0dec46e2fc03a9ab08d3a9b294",
      "text": "than the source it describes, and lossy by construction: whoever wrote it decided what mattered, and whatever they dropped is invisible to a reader who only has the summary.",
      "hash": "17ff9e8b467998b072ce2df48e410e38f4f11981a09aef067594c742ac3b0e99"
    },
    {
      "id": "fa1530c306b5b7bf3c98dcbd59f394d5bf0e52a7aac7744b850675b321c01e41",
      "text": "A lot of",
      "hash": "95a5b2f56f26e61aa6169019c280e959de67b08074f9fc7b4a20eaf5b7e64f8d"
    },
    {
      "id": "28de47d24fc7e8c5827e71066a57d84ca0a52b1ead367300d6f7279189b2346a",
      "text": "engineering is the manufacture of secondary sources.",
      "hash": "d9c622ff09709f81b423a8da8a6d71d4ca2a79fae5f87d4de6e848796f487a86"
    },
    {
      "id": "b215fd2122b97ccfaf05b39cb869d9935553895a4edbb2372cc164a3c93ebddb",
      "text": "Compaction",
      "hash": "a0ade140bc8e408639e51492b949bc4d31641625ef070015b5d4a5e92ef0edb0"
    },
    {
      "id": "276438816b4065ce79651ef3ef64544dec1650acb423fe04cc46b75408c05c40",
      "text": "turns the",
      "hash": "2f959563baf84f2b02af4185975b6225e185de70f15169968d5719fafbec8bc8"
    },
    {
      "id": "0e2f2a41e4ecb9aaf53731763e9e0e555e7d0bb7f71423f6495a022112b4dc48",
      "text": "history into a summary that seeds the next session. A",
      "hash": "45f02086f72c619c189f643c2890a50d61acd417a7577cdbb2bce179b7fba82f"
    },
    {
      "id": "2dbfcef949264f6b91c86d2f076dfe7867e5cc2f74c49b2d6ac603bbd0b71765",
      "text": "burns its own context on a noisy search and returns a short report. A",
      "hash": "668f56f16323b068ffc633bade5ff772e688942629afcf47aa921eda0ccb6506"
    },
    {
      "id": "967a3506f795a97287d46d5d6a7e73befa93a4cfdfe4aac53e73bd29e8bcbaa9",
      "text": "handoff artifact",
      "hash": "741619a26b388b5e1035994e6e7ce6c59c885ebd231ad21f8d9ff02438a0cbc9"
    },
    {
      "id": "947a06034ca3ca7eec338dbf4011009a057f6e2f3db7ce3426c22558c54e5d58",
      "text": "condenses a session's decisions into a document the next session reads.",
      "hash": "1f8524030d671a190f3cb4043888cfdec4681c5aac4734bda75a6dd387690abb"
    },
    {
      "id": "852a6bc8c84060b2d3400be7fd3eec4fa67c43b31e17b4c198c8ecadfe7aa692",
      "text": "Memory systems",
      "hash": "aef3f4f5b38818a0787d770984d5f5e8dc71f84aa9dc6983bbfc049fc6be2581"
    },
    {
      "id": "021e33fc6756645b1fedf83f139c8cf4699b81f6934d109f2cb6df7afebead00",
      "text": "distil what a session learned into notes. Each makes the same trade: fidelity for headroom.",
      "hash": "249104c73ed7809d8781fae14cd45a659656625260bf5613db4a9294195c4971"
    },
    {
      "id": "73ae4e65da32f1a67f03d9d4566529bc531436c957d1d6ab6845c7bcca523ac5",
      "text": "Secondary sources fail in two ways. They're lossy — the compaction summary that lost the schema decision, the report that didn't mention the edge case. And they drift — the primary source changes and the account doesn't follow, so docs describe last quarter's architecture with this quarter's confidence. When an",
      "hash": "67b74a3c81cf94c468339744c9f94e9af72657ebcf9487fcb6dbc12409649efe"
    },
    {
      "id": "4eaf5f07e3622bca34fcde529c92875cd76f358d86639dd4cb084682aa990848",
      "text": "acts on a secondary source that has failed either way, it works confidently from wrong information; the fix is sending it back to the primary source.",
      "hash": "668edb8d8f4868521025b9b26ba5c27bfd85d69f09cc63ea78c703af2bd5b988"
    },
    {
      "id": "b74d589654c9604bb36258956a459a1741fdaa2e60c69e6829f83cbffb12a8a6",
      "text": "Neither failure makes secondary sources a mistake. The context window is finite, and primary sources are expensive; without summaries, reports, and handoff documents, nothing large fits. The skill is knowing which details can survive the loss — and verifying against the primary source when one can't. A well-made secondary source carries a",
      "hash": "e06db6c60d3398b057dac76271807745e3fe63abb4216af8855be4003bb50190"
    },
    {
      "id": "f44c2edeadf90dbbc89499f6d534d5b9f4d8ea5f5b99610ec233b534a6836478",
      "text": "context pointer",
      "hash": "7fb80893d92cf9accaa94f3b2f011e80e1ed58eb0ec3e161e07b14e34c36ca1b"
    },
    {
      "id": "871737e69f3a5ea79e79ef918c96ab3a6cd791d90d7e3fd60a0dbddc72e3e61e",
      "text": "back to its original — the summary that names the transcript it came from, the doc that names the file it describes — so when the account isn't enough, the reader can follow the pointer rather than work from the loss.",
      "hash": "414da360466338ef677d774c48c1e7f0cc5fe2c7383deca768eaf390e37a56b7"
    },
    {
      "id": "e420508700e3e752d003334db4181c5ecad18ed47c30c394201c1922ee9cf363",
      "text": "Usage:",
      "hash": "2bad3eeaf33caffe3bc9b482b4934ed19eb4ec3614c12373e1a5c5f8948217da"
    },
    {
      "id": "43d85ca61ae1ce305fe1a84baa26e1f1c168643e608fb1b92a46cf7d693fe707",
      "text": "\"The handoff doc says auth is done, but the new session keeps finding broken token refresh.\"",
      "hash": "936e762df6362817a0ea217a222a8731873d5fafb5551a829642b73db09dc729"
    },
    {
      "id": "45dd8dcc4fcb4737642867327316762f0170d45664e049aa25ea71951c569214",
      "text": "\"The doc's a secondary source — the last session wrote down what it believed, not what's true. Have the new session run the auth tests and trust the primary source.\"",
      "hash": "5ba2ae02aa70bb45f93ff63367f1900cfa4909ad91774cc6194a86980aaad417"
    },
    {
      "id": "07a8e8ccdfee46b50fac5d5f1c3a901d430556fe7640a29a60aa1db3110bda71",
      "text": "Previous term",
      "hash": "735604aff9e8f2192b83df4905cfc8e395613e0ce05f8ca85a1d2d1d44fd59f3"
    },
    {
      "id": "4d39df7eb98d9de581c3065e654be3933cc5305309071c852d96b48539374684",
      "text": "Primary source",
      "hash": "a518c683cac9ab4d00390db41fe8a1fb150258d23d103dec32e0017ff94a0b5d"
    },
    {
      "id": "0eb3dba7093f725e3cb7f0beb69f5c3ea88bdf2cb6dce235b9d0f0b47eddf031",
      "text": "Next term",
      "hash": "5219c7ebdc0e098aa6db6f09e405c1b17ab75f1082862906a872e10a16818f9e"
    },
    {
      "id": "ab85d6027ce64afdb04e8d22a856a6a1fa359d52521fd3750eef8b93e4c82881",
      "text": "Handoff artifact",
      "hash": "ead240861579b1a7860feadb4392025d981ee640559b4a3c75c64eba36517a48"
    },
    {
      "id": "996d6c03640d04ed4c64200c196246b82583f4ca07cc8b3fa93d6808daf5c709",
      "text": "Want more than vocabulary?",
      "hash": "5d5500a083006a1606e84a03c018904d01364631c6baea4c7a3f8f3f62bf94dc"
    },
    {
